  "_about": "What each AI nation sets out to do in Historical mode, by turn (turn 1 is September 1939). These are intentions, not results: the armies still have to win the battles. declare lists nations the AI declares war on that turn. posture is attack, defend or redeploy. objectives are worked through in order. axis is the line the tanks are massed along. haltOrder is ground the plan leaves alone in its first month (the stop short of Dunkirk, and Paris until the second phase). lastPush names prizes that troops who close up to them late in the month go straight in against, instead of waiting a month at the gates. staging keeps a few corps at a jumping-off point. landings sends named corps across the sea, each to the first place on its list it can get ashore: an enemy coast is assaulted (only at fair odds if it is defended), an ally's port is reinforced, and the corps stays overseas until the phase ends. fleets gives named fleets their orders for the phase. minOdds lets a nation attack at worse odds than a careful staff would accept. declareWhenCollapsing waits until that nation is breaking, or has fallen.",
